{
  "id": "murphy-paranormal-shakti-onsite-amygdala",
  "name": "Paranormal Shakti on-site: amygdala signal, 8-coil cross ('Lady Vampire')",
  "category": "presence",
  "evidence": "claim",
  "origin": "Todd Murphy (Paranormal Shakti software, retired)",
  "uT": 1,
  "summary": "The on-site amygdala session of Murphy's retired Paranormal Shakti (about 2012-2015), which the vendor sold to paranormal investigators to raise their 'sensitivity' at a site: 30 min of the amygdala signal alternating between the two stereo channels of a 4-coil cross on each temporal lobe. The vendor links it to the 'Lady Vampire' episode of the TV series Paranormal State.",
  "setting": "On site during an investigation (vendor).",
  "schedule": "Vendor: after 6 temporal sessions, do 3 frontal ones (murphy-paranormal-shakti-frontal), but not in the 3 days before an investigation, because it says the frontal session lowers sensitivity. The vendor's general Shakti rules: at most every 72 h or once a week, never on consecutive days.",
  "notes": "Coils form a cross on each temporal lobe: FT7 (front), C5 (top), TP7 (back) and T9 (bottom) on the left, FT8, C6, TP8 and T10 on the right; the sites are an inference from the vendor's description. Following 'begin with the left channel vertical and the right channel horizontal', track 1 (the left stereo channel) drives the top and bottom coils (C5, T9, C6, T10) and track 2 (the right channel) the front and back coils (FT7, TP7, FT8, TP8). The signal alternates between the two groups slowly, one whole signal per switch with about 4 s of silence in between; the Paranormal Shakti pages give no alternation speed, and the 8 Coil Shakti's 'fast' mode (a switch every half-second), which its pages say 'emerged as the most effective' in the original developers' lab tests, is not used. Polarity follows the 8 Coil Shakti coil chart (the Paranormal Shakti pages do not repeat it): each pair is one + and one - coil, so C5 (top) and FT7 (front) on the left and T10 (bottom) and TP8 (back) on the right get the reversed signal (weight -1), while T9, TP7, C6 and FT8 get it as is. The amygdala ('burstx') file is proprietary; it is approximated by the built-in accelerating burst (6 to 30 Hz, 230 points of 3 ms = 0.69 s, after the published 230-point burst-firing pattern). For the TV episode the vendor says 'the coils were placed about two inches forward of their usual locations' (move the whole cross about 5 cm forward). The vendor also describes the cross 'raised up' above the temporo-parietal region. Experiences during or after such a session are not evidence about the site. Persinger's lab reported that burst-firing fields over the right temporoparietal region raised hypnotic suggestibility (Healey 1996) and that three weekly bilateral sessions increased aggression (Gillis & Persinger 1993). An independent sham-controlled test of the 8 Coil Shakti amygdala signal found no effect on emotional responses (Gendle & McGrath 2012), and a double-blind God Helmet test found no field effect (Granqvist 2005). The product is retired; this file is of historical interest. Not for people with epilepsy; stop at once on fear or distress.",
  "targets": [
    "left-amygdala",
    "right-amygdala"
  ],
  "source": "Murphy, Paranormal Shakti: on-site sessions (Wayback, 2013) https://web.archive.org/web/20130509035301/http://www.shaktitechnology.com/Paranormal_Shakti/paranormal_demo/on-site_sessions.htm ; Murphy, Paranormal Shakti: the procedure (Wayback, 2013) https://web.archive.org/web/20130509035643/http://www.shaktitechnology.com/Paranormal_Shakti/paranormal_demo/the_procedure.htm ; Murphy, Paranormal Shakti: frontal lobe session (Wayback, 2013) https://web.archive.org/web/20130509021211/http://www.shaktitechnology.com/Paranormal_Shakti/paranormal_demo/Frontal_lobe_consent.htm ; Murphy, Comments on the Lady Vampire episode of Paranormal State http://www.innerworlds.50megs.com/paranormal_state.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Getting Started (8-coil chart, +/- coil pairs) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/getting_started_basic.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Understanding the 8 Coil Shakti (fast and slow alternation) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/rot_principles.htm ; Murphy, Shakti demo: What are 'Rapid' and 'High-Speed' signals? (3-ms points, 4-s latency) https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/rapid_&_high_speed_signals.htm ; Ryczko & Persinger 2002, Percept Mot Skills 95:592 (230-point burst-firing pattern) https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/12434855/ ; Healey, Persinger & Koren 1996, Int J Neurosci 87:201 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/9003980/ ; Gillis & Persinger 1993, Percept Mot Skills 76:168 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/8451123/ ; Murphy, Shakti demo: Safety - how often https://www.god-helmet.com/wp/winshakti/demo/shakti_demo/how_often_is_safe.htm ; Gendle & McGrath 2012, Percept Mot Skills 114:217 (8 Coil Shakti amygdala signal, sham-controlled) https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/22582690/ ; Granqvist et al. 2005, Neurosci Lett 379:1 https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/15849873/",
